            "faqBadge": "FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS",
            "faqTitleIntro": "Frequently Asked",
            "faqTitleHighlight": "Questions",
            "faqDescription": "Explore common questions regarding our turnaround times, process, deliverables, and engineering standards.",
            "faqSchemaMarkup": "<script type=\"application/ld+json\">\n{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@type\": \"FAQPage\",\n  \"mainEntity\": [\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"How much do graphic design services cost?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"It depends on scope, not a flat rate. A single logo sits at one end, a full brand system with packaging and collateral sits at the other. A standalone logo costs less than a complete identity build. Bundled projects (brand kit, social, packaging) are priced as packages. We quote clearly after a short discovery call, with no hidden add ons. You only ever pay for the design you will actually use.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"What is included in brand identity design?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"A full identity is a system, not just a logo. It usually covers everything your brand needs to look consistent everywhere. Primary logo plus variations and a favicon Color palette and typography system Usage rules and a brand guidelines sheet Source files in print and web formats The goal is a kit that keeps your brand sharp on any surface.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"How long does a design project take?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Most projects run two to four weeks, based on scope. A single logo moves quicker, while a full identity with packaging takes longer because more pieces need to line up. We share a clear timeline upfront and keep you posted at every stage, so you are never left wondering where things stand.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"Do I own the design and get the source files?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Yes, you own the final work, full stop. On completion you get editable source files (AI, PSD, PDF, and web ready formats), so you are never locked in or charged just to make a future edit. Owning your assets means you can scale, print, or hand them to another team whenever you like.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"Should I hire a freelancer or a graphic design agency?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"It depends on how much you need and how reliable it has to be. A freelancer can handle one off tasks, but a graphic design agency brings range, consistency, and backup when deadlines get tight. Freelancers suit small, single skill jobs. An agency covers branding, social, print, and web in one place. You get accountability and steady quality across every asset. For anything tied to growth, a full service team usually pays for itself.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"How many revisions do I get?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Revisions are built into every project, never billed as a surprise. We refine together until the work fits your brand and goals, within a fair, clearly stated number of rounds so the process stays focused. That back and forth is exactly how we land on a result you are genuinely happy to put your name on.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"Can you redesign my brand without losing recognition?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Yes, a smart refresh updates your look without erasing it. As a careful creative design agency, we protect the equity you have already built and modernize the rest. We spot the cues your audience already recognizes, keep those, and refresh everything around them, so the new identity feels current yet still clearly yours.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"Do you design for both print and digital?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Yes, we cover both and keep them aligned. From business cards and packaging to social graphics and website assets, your visuals stay consistent whether someone holds them or scrolls past them. One unified look across print and digital makes your brand feel bigger, tighter, and far more trustworthy.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"How do I choose between a graphic design agency near me and a remote team?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Choose on results and process, not just how close the office is. A “graphic design agency near me” search feels safer, but remote teams often bring wider skill and better value when the workflow is solid. Judge portfolio quality over location. Check communication, timelines, and the revision policy. Confirm you will own the files no matter who you hire. A strong process beats a nearby address every time.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"How do graphic design services actually increase sales?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"By removing friction and building trust before a single word is read. Clean visuals make offers clearer, brands feel more credible, and calls to action impossible to miss, and clarity plus trust is what turns browsers into buyers. Done right, great design does not just look better, it quietly guides more people toward saying yes.\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n</script>",
