            "faqDescription": "Explore common questions regarding our turnaround times, process, deliverables, and engineering standards.",
            "faqSchemaMarkup": "<script type=\"application/ld+json\">\n{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@type\": \"FAQPage\",\n  \"mainEntity\": [\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"How much does it cost to build an app in 2026?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Pricing for our app development services depends on complexity and the features desired. General guidelines follow: Simple apps using basic features cost less and ship faster. Cross-platform build typically costs 30-50% less than two separate native apps. Custom backends, integrations, and real-time data requests add to the budget. Our quotes are clear and itemized. Expect no surprise charges once work begins.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"How long does it take to build an app?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"The time to develop most apps is between two and five months. The time is less to develop a focused version of the app, and features rich apps naturally take longer to develop. We follow a development methodology that improves visibility, so you can track the development status and estimated time to achieve key milestones.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"Should I build a native or cross-platform app?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"For most businesses, cross-platform is the better option to start with: Cost and time savings since reach is both platforms from a single codebase. For most apps, near-native speed is achievable. When deep hardware features or Augmented Reality are required, native is better We weigh your goals honestly and recommend the path that fits your product, not the one that bills the most.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"Do you build for both iOS and Android?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"We do. We are a full-service app design and development company. We can cover both platforms quickly and effectively with a single cross-platform codebase or with neat native apps for each, using either or both. Since most app spending comes from Apple users and Android has the most global market share, both platforms offer the best market and spending reach for your app.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"What happens after my app launches?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Launch is the beginning, not the end. Apps need ongoing care to stay healthy: Regular updates for new phones and OS versions. Security patches to protect users and their data. Bug fixes and improvements based on real usage. Steady maintenance keeps your ratings high and your users loyal, since neglected apps quietly lose both over time.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"I only have an idea, not designs. Can you still help?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Of course, and this is the case for most of our clients. We take ideas and turn them into actionable steps. Soon after that, we develop digital prototypes that can be interacted with to simulate the user experience. Catching design faults at this stage is much less expensive. We do the rest; we just need your goal.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"Will I own the source code and my app?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Yes, completely. You own your app, your source code, and every related asset. As a transparent custom app development services provider, we believe what you pay for belongs to you, with no lock-in and no hostage situations. You are always free to grow, transfer, or expand your app on your own terms.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"How do you stop app costs from spiraling?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Surprise invoices come from poor planning, so we plan tightly: We define clear scope and deliverables before building. We prototype first to catch issues while changes are cheap. We work in stages, with your sign-off at each one. This keeps spending predictable and tied to real value, so your budget builds a strong app, not avoidable rework.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"Can you fix or rebuild an app that's already broken?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Yes. Inheriting a crashing, slow, or outdated app is common, and very fixable. A capable app development company can audit your existing build, find what is draining performance, and either repair it or rebuild it on cleaner, faster foundations. Many of our best results come from rescuing apps others gave up on.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"How do you make sure people keep using the app?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Retention is designed in, not hoped for. Since most apps lose the bulk of their users within a month, we focus hard on what brings people back: Fast load times that pass the five-second test. Simple flows that guide users straight to action. Rigorous testing so crashes never push people away. The result is an app people open, trust, and keep, long after install day.\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n</script>",
