            "strategy": {
              "enabled": true,
              "eyebrow": "04 // HOW IT WORKS",
              "titleIntro": "What A Logo Really Does Once It Is",
              "titleHighlight": "Out In The Wild",
              "description": "People often reference logos as the first impression of a company. The right logo leads to trust and quality association, helping to capture your audience. Professional logo design can help you capture potential clients by trust and a call to action. You have five seconds to capture a customer. Without a professionally designed logo, you run the risk of losing out on a customer base.\n\nThe perception of most customers is that a poorly designed logo is the first step in a poorly run business. Logos should never be treated as decoration. Consider them a 24/7 employee, working to advertise your business. Logos should always create an inviting brand that brings customers in.\n\nHere is how we make a mark pull its weight:",
              "components": [
                {
                  "num": "01",
                  "title": "Instant Recognition",
                  "desc": "Shape and color have to stick first. We design clean, simple marks the brain stores fast, since a single signature color can lift brand recognition by as much as 80%."
                },
                {
                  "num": "02",
                  "title": "Earned Trust",
                  "desc": "Neat lines, balanced spacing, and the right font quietly tell buyers you are careful and established, which makes them comfortable spending money with you."
